{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5607) that requires implementing four specific SRD requirements for `cmd/df` (filesystem disk space usage reporter):\n   - **R1.5**: Column widths must be computed as per-column maxima across all rows including headers, matching GNU df alignment. Fields separated by at least one space.\n   - **R2.1**: `-h` / `--human-readable` flag to display sizes using binary units (1024-based: K, M, G, T, P, E) via `pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})`. Column header changes from \"1K-blocks\" to \"Size\". Applies to Size, Used, and Available columns.\n   - **R2.2**: `-H` / `--si` flag to display sizes using SI units (1000-based: kB, MB, GB, TB, PB, EB) via `pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})`. Column header changes from \"1K-blocks\" to \"Size\". Applies to Size, Used, Available columns.\n   - **R2.3**: `-h` and `-H` are mutually exclusive; the last one on the command line takes precedence.\n   \n   The task specifies: modify `cmd/df/main.go` and `cmd/df/df_test.go`, do not rewrite from scratch, add differential tests for each requirement, verify with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary vs `gdf` (Homebrew GNU df)\n   - `pkg/format.HumanSize(bytes int64, opts HumanSizeOpts) string` for human-readable formatting\n   - `format.HumanSizeOpts{Binary: bool}` - true for 1024-based (K,M,G), false for 1000-based (kB,MB,GB)\n   - `format.PadRight` / `format.PadLeft` for column alignment\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - `unix.Getfsstat` / `unix.Statfs_t` for Darwin filesystem enumeration\n   - Fixed `[6]string` arrays for column headers and entry data\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for all test cases\n   - No git commands allowed - orchestrator manages git externally\n   - E8: No function may exceed 40 lines\n   - Write all files before building/testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd106-df.yaml** (full SRD read)\n     - Defines all df requirements R1.1-R4.3\n     - R1.5: Column width alignment matching GNU df\n     - R2.1: `-h`/`--human-readable` binary units via format.HumanSize\n     - R2.2: `-H`/`--si` SI units via format.HumanSize\n     - R2.3: Last `-h`/`-H` wins when both present\n     - Non-goals include: --sync, --total, -P, --block-size, -k (accepted but no effect)\n     - Package contract imports: pkg/format, pkg/sys\n\n   - **cmd/df/main.go** (existing implementation, 248 lines, implements R1.1-R1.4)\n     - Key structures and functions:\n     ```go\n     type fsEntry struct {\n         filesystem string\n         blocks1K   int64\n         used       int64\n         available  int64\n         usePercent string\n         mountedOn  string\n     }\n     \n     var headers = [6]string{\n         \"Filesystem\", \"1K-blocks\", \"Used\", \"Available\", \"Use%\", \"Mounted on\",\n     }\n     ```\n     - `run(args []string) int` - no flag parsing, only checks empty args\n     - `buildEntry(stat unix.Statfs_t) fsEntry` - converts block sizes to 1K units\n     - `computeWidths(entries []fsEntry) [6]int` - per-column max widths (R1.5 already partially implemented)\n     - `printLine(cols [6]string, w [6]int)` - formats one row with PadRight/PadLeft\n     - `entryStrings(e fsEntry) [6]string` - converts fsEntry to string columns\n     - `computeUsePercent(total, avail int64) string` - ceiling percentage calculation\n     - Already imports: fmt, math, os, strconv, strings, syscall, pkg/format, pkg/sys, unix\n\n   - **cmd/df/df_test.go** (existing test file, 55 lines)\n     ```go\n     func programNameNormalizer(b []byte) []byte {\n         return bytes.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"gdf:\"), []byte(\"df:\"))\n     }\n     \n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gdf\")\n         if err != nil {\n             t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n         }\n         errNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{programNameNormalizer}\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n             {Name: \"root-fs\", Args: []string{\"/\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n             {Name: \"file-arg\", Args: []string{\"/etc/hosts\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n             {Name: \"multiple-files\", Args: []string{\"/\", \"/tmp\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n             {Name: \"nonexistent\", Args: []string{\"/nonexistent-path-12345\"}, ExitCode: 1, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}, Normalize: errNorm},\n             {Name: \"mixed-valid-invalid\", Args: []string{\"/\", \"/nonexistent-path-12345\"}, ExitCode: 1, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}, Normalize: errNorm},\n             {Name: \"duplicate-file\", Args: []string{\"/\", \"/\"}, Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=C\"}},\n         }\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n     - Uses `gdf` as reference binary\n     - Has `programNameNormalizer` to replace \"gdf:\" with \"df:\" in error output\n     - 6 existing test cases covering R1.1-R1.4\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only read three files before being interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R1.5 (column width alignment) appears partially implemented already via `computeWidths` which computes per-column maxima including headers. May need verification that it matches GNU df exactly.\n   - The main challenge is implementing R2.1/R2.2/R2.3 which require:\n     1. Command-line flag parsing (currently none exists)\n     2. Tracking display mode (default/human-readable/SI)\n     3. Storing raw byte values for human-readable conversion (currently only 1K-block values stored)\n     4. Dynamic header changing (\"1K-blocks\" → \"Size\")\n     5. Last-flag-wins semantics for -h/-H mutual exclusivity\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The massive task prompt with all project context, SRD specifications, execution constitution, coding standards, and specific task requirements for implementing srd106 R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 in cmd/df.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation for context preservation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R1.5 (verify/fix column width alignment to match GNU df)\n   - Implement R2.1 (-h/--human-readable flag with binary unit display)\n   - Implement R2.2 (-H/--si flag with SI unit display)\n   - Implement R2.3 (last -h/-H wins mutual exclusivity)\n   - Add differential test cases for each requirement\n   - Verify: `go build ./cmd/df/`, `go vet ./cmd/df/`, `go test ./cmd/df/ -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the three required files (SRD, main.go, df_test.go) and was about to begin the implementation phase. I stated: \"I'll start by reading the SRD for df to understand requirements R1.5, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, then read the existing implementation files.\" All three reads completed successfully. The next step was to plan the approach and write the code changes.\n\n   Key implementation decisions needed:\n   - Need to add flag parsing to `run()` function - must handle `-h`, `--human-readable`, `-H`, `--si` with last-wins semantics\n   - The `fsEntry` struct needs raw byte values (not just 1K-blocks) for human-readable formatting, OR compute bytes from 1K values at format time (multiply by 1024)\n   - `entryStrings()` needs to become mode-aware to format sizes differently\n   - Headers need to be dynamic (not a fixed global var) when -h/-H is active\n   - `printTable` and related functions need to accept the display mode\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement all code changes in `cmd/df/main.go` and `cmd/df/df_test.go` in a single pass, then build and test. Specifically:\n   \n   1. Add a display mode type and flag parsing to `run()` that walks args manually to support last-wins semantics for -h/-H\n   2. Modify `fsEntry` to store raw byte values alongside 1K-block values (or compute from blocks1K * 1024)\n   3. Make `entryStrings` and header generation mode-aware, calling `format.HumanSize(bytes, format.HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true/false})` for -h/-H modes\n   4. Add test cases: `{Name: \"human-readable\", Args: []string{\"-h\", \"/\"}}`, `{Name: \"si-units\", Args: []string{\"-H\", \"/\"}}`, `{Name: \"last-h-wins\", Args: []string{\"-H\", \"-h\", \"/\"}}`, `{Name: \"last-H-wins\", Args: []string{\"-h\", \"-H\", \"/\"}}`, and an alignment test for R1.5\n   5. Run `go build -o bin/df ./cmd/df/`, `go vet ./cmd/df/`, `go test ./cmd/df/ -count=1`\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd106 requirement R1.5 per the SRD\", \"Implement srd106 requirement R2.1 per the SRD\", \"Implement srd106 requirement R2.2 per the SRD\", \"Implement srd106 requirement R2.3 per the SRD\" with acceptance criteria requiring compilation, all tests passing, at least one differential test per requirement, and go vet clean.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5607/23c1c290-2627-430c-aa84-94704d0f6b79.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23c1c290-2627-430c-aa84-94704d0f6b79","uuid":"14f111d5-1d5a-4180-aea5-6