ers) using `utf8.RuneCountInString()`.\n\n---\n\n### Other Exported Functions and Types\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5607/pkg/format/pad.go`\n- `Columns(entries []string, termWidth int) [][]string` (Lines 35-41): Arranges entries into a grid that fits within termWidth columns, filling top-to-bottom, left-to-right with 2-space gap\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5607/pkg/format/color.go`\n- `FileTypeColor(mode os.FileMode) string` (Lines 39-61): Returns ANSI escape sequence for a file's type\n- `Reset() string` (Lines 65-70): Returns ANSI reset sequence\n- `ColorEnabled(w io.Writer) bool` (Lines 74-88): Reports whether color output is enabled for the given writer\n- `SetColorEnabled(enabled bool)` (Lines 92-96): Forces color output on or off regardless of terminal detection\n- `ResetColorEnabled()` (Lines 100-104): Clears any color override, restoring terminal-based detection\n\n**Files:** `align.go` and `columns.go` are empty (package declaration only)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23c1c290-2627-430c-aa84-94704d0f6b79","uuid":"30383344-a9b8-474e-bac7-45689cebb7d7","timestamp":"2026-05-27T19:46:33.981Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find the HumanSize function and HumanSizeOpts type in pkg/format/. I need the exact function signature, the struct fields of HumanSizeOpts, and how PadLeft/PadRight work. Report the file paths, line numbers, and full signatures. Also check if there are any other exported functions or types I should know about. Be thorough - check all .go files in pkg/format/.","agentId":"a62e0b630bc2a4ed3","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good. Now let me create a comprehensive summary based on the files I've read:\n\n## Summary of pkg/format/\n\nHere's the complete information you requested:\n\n### HumanSize Function\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt